---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const lines = [
  "Every project starts the same way: an empty file and too many tabs open.",
  "",
  "This one's a blog. Not because the world needs another one, but because",
  "writing things down is the cheapest debugger I know. Half the bugs I've",
  "fixed, I fixed while typing out the problem for someone else — usually",
  "before I even finished the sentence.",
  "",
  "## What this is",
  "",
  "A place for the small, specific things: a bug that took four hours and",
  "turned out to be a timezone; a refactor that made a file worse before",
  "it made it better; a tool that quietly changed how I work.",
  "",
  "Nothing here will be a definitive guide. It's a log, not a lecture.",
  "",
  "## What this isn't",
  "",
  "It isn't going to be polished. Some posts will be three paragraphs.",
  "Some will have code that I later realize was wrong. That's fine —",
  "the commit history stays visible on purpose.",
  "",
  "## Why now",
  "",
  "No good reason, honestly. The domain was free, the terminal was open,",
  "and `git init` felt easier than the alternative, which was doing",
  "nothing.",
  "",
  "> The best time to start a changelog was a year ago.",
  "> The second best time is right after you buy the domain.",
  "",
  "More soon.",
];
---
<BaseLayout title="Hello, World — your blog" tabLabel="hello-world.md" current="hello-world">
  <div class="content">
    <p class="article-meta">~/blog/posts $ cat hello-world.md</p>
    <article class="article">
      <div class="gutter">
        {lines.map((_, i) => <div>{i + 1}</div>)}
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <h1>Hello, World</h1>
        {lines.map(line => {
          if (line.startsWith('## ')) return <h2>{line.replace('## ', '')}</h2>;
          if (line.startsWith('> ')) return <blockquote>{line.replace('> ', '')}</blockquote>;
          if (line.trim() === '') return null;
          return <p>{line}</p>;
        })}
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
